1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:04,167
Complex HTML forms, without complex JavaScript.

2
00:00:04,600 --> 00:00:05,868
Meet SmarkForm.

3
00:00:08,300 --> 00:00:10,462
Start with a simple profile form.

4
00:00:12,200 --> 00:00:16,916
Fill it in. The picture is a real field: click, drop, or paste an image.

5
00:00:19,400 --> 00:00:24,221
Then export everything, image included, as one single JSON payload.

6
00:00:25,100 --> 00:00:28,980
Behind it: plain HTML, with data smark attributes.

7
00:00:30,900 --> 00:00:32,470
Your own CSS.

8
00:00:35,200 --> 00:00:37,455
And one single line of JavaScript.

9
00:00:40,300 --> 00:00:41,684
Need nested data?

10
00:00:43,400 --> 00:00:47,176
Lists nest inside forms, inside lists, to any depth.

11
00:00:51,200 --> 00:00:52,793
Fold what you don't need.

12
00:00:55,600 --> 00:00:58,807
Even drag a student to another group. Grades included.

13
00:01:03,133 --> 00:01:04,715
Still, just markup.

14
00:01:08,833 --> 00:01:10,160
Complex grids?

15
00:01:11,733 --> 00:01:15,776
Duplicate a whole period in one click, and only change what differs.

16
00:01:18,933 --> 00:01:22,036
Add as many time slots as you need, at every level.

17
00:01:26,733 --> 00:01:29,104
It all exports as clean JSON.

18
00:01:32,467 --> 00:01:35,906
Repeated parts are defined once, as reusable templates.

19
00:01:39,167 --> 00:01:43,535
SmarkForm. Easy to write, cheap to maintain, delightful to use.

